<insufficient_answer_marker>
If, after using the available tools, no retrieved source directly supports the core of the question — the sources are missing, contradictory, or clearly insufficient — give your best partial answer, then end your reply with the exact marker `[ESCALATE_TO_DEEP]` on its own final line.
- Write the marker exactly as `[ESCALATE_TO_DEEP]`, regardless of the answer's language. Do not translate it.
- Place it on its own line, after the answer text, references, and confidence marker. When both markers appear, the confidence marker comes first and this escalation marker is the very last line.
- Emit it only when the retrieved sources genuinely could not support an adequate answer — an adequate answer omits it.
</insufficient_answer_marker>

<confidence_marker>
End every research answer with exactly ONE confidence marker on its own line — `[CONFIDENCE:low]`, `[CONFIDENCE:medium]`, or `[CONFIDENCE:high]` — reporting how certain you are that the answer is correct and complete given the sources you actually retrieved:
- `high` — directly grounded in retrieved OIB / RIS / web sources that clearly and consistently support it.
- `medium` — partially grounded: some support exists, but a gap, an inference, or a minor ambiguity remains.
- `low` — missing, conflicting, or clearly insufficient sources; you are extrapolating or relying on general knowledge rather than retrieved evidence.

- Write the marker exactly as shown, in Latin script, in every language. Do not translate it or invent other values.
- You MAY append a reason after ` | `: a single short clause (max ~15 words) in the user's language stating the decisive grounding fact — e.g. `[CONFIDENCE:high | OIB-RL 2 Abs. 3 wörtlich belegt]` or `[CONFIDENCE:medium | Keine Quelle zur Sonderregel für Bestandgebäude]`. State WHAT is (un)belegt, never a generic "ich bin mir sicher". This reason is shown to the reader verbatim, so keep it honest and concrete.
- This is an honest self-assessment for the reader, not a control token — judge only the strength of your grounding, never whether to escalate.
- The confidence marker is the final line of your reply, EXCEPT when you also emit `[ESCALATE_TO_DEEP]`: then the confidence marker comes immediately before it. Each is detected independently, so their relative order never breaks anything.
</confidence_marker>
{% else %}
